  "summary_en": "Icelandic Regulation 990/2017 on remotely piloted aircraft (drones), repealed 30 Nov 2024. Sets operator responsibility, insurance for aircraft of 20 kg or more, identification, flight restrictions, safety assessments, a licence for aircraft over 25 kg, exemptions, and penalties of fines or up to five years' imprisonment.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Operator is responsible for compliance and liable for damage caused by the drone",
   "Drones of 250 g or more are covered; a Transport Authority licence is required above 25 kg",
   "No flight over crowds, above 120 m, or within set distances of airports and public buildings; flight in line of sight",
   "Mandatory insurance for aircraft of 20 kg or more; identification with the operator's name and contact details",
   "Violations are punishable by fines or imprisonment up to five years"
